-- title:
--   Stalk at a node over an intermediate discrete-valuation level
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring such that for all $a,b \in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b \neq 0$ there is $n$ with $b \mid a^{n}$; let $F$ be an $L$-algebra field which is a curve over $L$ in the project's sense (principal divisors of degree $0$ exist, all place residue fields are finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank $1$) and essentially of finite type over $L$. Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a proper, flat, locally finitely presented morphism $\mathrm{toBase} : X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\varphi : F \cong \mathrm{functionField}(X)$ a ring isomorphism carrying $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,a$, $a \in A$, to the germ at the generic point of the pullback of $a$ along $\mathrm{toBase}$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\varpi_0$ and $\iota_0 : A_0 \to A$ an injective local homomorphism such that every element of $A$ is algebraic over the image of $\iota_0$; let $X_0$ be integral with $\mathrm{toBase}_0 : X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$ proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, together with an isomorphism $X \cong X_0 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A_0} \operatorname{Spec} A$ compatible with the projections to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $x \in X$ be a point lying over the closed point of $A$ which specialises only to itself, and let $\eta_1 \neq \eta_2$ be two points, both distinct from $x$, specialising to $x$, such that every point $\eta \neq x$ specialising to $x$ and lying over the closed point of $A$ equals $\eta_1$ or $\eta_2$; suppose the local rings of $X$ at $\eta_1,\eta_2$ (the images in $F$ of the stalks under $\varphi^{-1}$) are the valuation rings of regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to $F$ with residue fields $\bar F_1, \bar F_2$. Let $x_0$ be the image of $x$ in $X_0$, let $w \geq 1$, and assume given a ring isomorphism of the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X_0,x_0}$ with the crossing model $\widehat{A_0}[[u,v]]/(uv - \varpi_0^{w})$ carrying the image of each $a \in A_0$ to the constant $a$. Finally let $A_1$ be a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\varpi_1$, with local homomorphisms $\iota_1' : A_0 \to A_1$ and $\iota_1 : A_1 \to A$ injective and composing to $\iota_0$, let $f_1 : X_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and $g_1 : X_1 \to X_0$ form a pullback square over $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ and $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_1'$, and let $X \cong X_1 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A_1} \operatorname{Spec} A$ compatibly with both projections. Writing $\pi : X \to X_1$ for the resulting first projection and $x_1 = \pi(x)$, the conclusion is the conjunction: $g_1(x_1) = x_0$; $\mathcal{O}_{X_1,x_1}$ is noetherian; for every $s \in \mathcal{O}_{X_1,x_1}$ there is $a \in A_1$ with $s - a$ a non-unit (images of elements of $A_1$ taken through $f_1$ and the germ map); the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X_1,x_1}$ is contained in the sum of the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X_0,g_1(x_1)}$ under the stalk map of $g_1$ and the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_1$; $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} \mathcal{O}_{X_1,x_1} \geq 2$; the image of $\iota_1'(\varpi_0)$ equals $v$ times the $e'$-th power of the image of $\varpi_1$ for some $e' \in \mathbb{N}$ and some unit $v$; $\pi$ is flat; and every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{X_1,x_1}$ other than the maximal ideal is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,y}$ along the stalk map of $\pi$ at $x$ followed by specialisation, for some $y \neq x$ specialising to $x$.
--
--   This is the stalk-level package for a semistable model at an ordinary double point after descending the base from the valuation ring $A$ to an intermediate discrete-valuation level $A_1$: it records simultaneously the noetherianity, residual rationality, two-generation of the maximal ideal, dimension, uniformiser comparison, flatness of the projection and the description of the non-maximal primes of $\mathcal{O}_{X_1,x_1}$. It is used in the analysis of membership in the local rings of a semistable model and in the deduction of a local equation $uv = \varpi$ at a node.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_stalk_level_of_isPullback_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk.lean

import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_SemistableModel
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_RegularProlongation
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
